WEBVTT

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.240
Hi, I'm Finian Joyce, chief fire officer from Leitrim in

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:06.800
Ireland. This new campaign, called European Smoke Alarm

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:09.880
Day, is a very welcome addition to the activities of

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:11.760
European Fire Safety Week.

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:14.320
It's great to see the collaboration on this campaign

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:17.160
between the European Fire Safety Alliance and the

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:19.240
Federation of European Fire Officers.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:23.000
I am aware that many services around Europe organise

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.560
campaigns individually in their own countries to promote

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:28.360
the installation of smoke alarms,

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:32.400
but this is the first time that European fire services have

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:35.560
come together to promote greater awareness about smoke

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:38.960
alarms. For many years we here in Ireland have regulations

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:42.520
in place in relation to smoke alarms in domestic homes,

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:46.280
and no doubt this has helped to save many lives.

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:49.040
I'm delighted to offer the support of the Irish Chief Fire

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:51.760
Officers for this new European campaign,

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:55.360
and would like to see more countries in Europe making it

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:58.680
mandatory to install smoke alarms in domestic homes.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:02.400
My final message to householders is to say that this little

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:06.246
piece of equipment can make a real difference in your lives.

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:09.899
Install smoke alarms in your homes today.